+# Certified Controller Specification & Test Matrix (Template)
+
+Purpose
+- Define the functional / non-functional requirements and tests required to certify torque-level and whole-body controllers for humanoid robots.
+
+Sections
+- Scope: torque-level control, whole-body balancing, contact handling, emergency stop, safe-stop transitions.
+- Safety levels: map functions to SIL/ASIL or SOTIF categories; operator to fill per-robot.
+- Requirements: deterministic timing (p99 latency), bounded jitter, watchdog times, command validation, safe trajectories, redundancy.
+- Test matrix:
+  - Jitter & latency: jitter_test (p99) at target loop frequency (500/1000/2000 Hz)
+  - Functional motion tests: pre-defined trajectories executed on robot & sim
+  - Fault injection: sensor drop, delayed IMU, packet loss, actuator saturation
+  - Stress: prolonged motion, thermal/power degradation
+  - Regression: compare torque trajectories vs golden traces in sim
+- Evidence & artifacts:
+  - Signed HIL run artifacts, logs, Prometheus metrics, recorded waveforms, simulation vs hardware comparisons
+  - Formal analysis artifacts for controller invariants (if available)
+- Acceptance criteria:
+  - All safety-relevant tests pass; signed evidence manifests exist for each test; third-party auditor signoff recorded.
+
+Operator actions:
+- Fill in service-level SLOs, target frequencies, thresholds and execute HIL campaigns per ops/robotics/certification/run_hil_tests.sh
